GW-BASIC 2026 for DOS

BIN/GWBASIC.EXE is the 16-bit real-mode interpreter. It needs no DOS extender.
Run GWBASIC to open the editor, or GWBASIC GAME.BAS to load and run a program.
Type SYSTEM to exit. The separate 32-bit build requires DOS4GW.EXE.

The package uses relative APPINFO, BIN, DOC and SOURCE directories. Extract
it into your chosen DOS software directory and put its BIN directory on PATH.
GWBASIC.EXE can share a filename with an older interpreter; choose a separate
installation directory if you want to retain both.

SOURCE/GWBASIC/SOURCE.TGZ contains the full tracked source tree. Extract it
on a host with long-filename support to preserve the original source names.
The installed interpreter and outer package entries use 8.3 filenames.
The native-code compiler is a separate POSIX tool; it is not in this DOS binary.

See README for building, CHANGES for updates and LICENSE for the MIT licence.
The source archive includes the separate Unlicense for BASIC Computer Games.
Hardware interfaces include emulation and stubs. Floating-point arithmetic
uses IEEE 754; it is not identical to the original Microsoft intermediate math.

Project: https://github.com/evvaletov/gw-basic-2026
